    "q-13813": {
      "dom_id": "step-q13813",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{6}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\int \\frac{1}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {u}^{-1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
