    "q-31400": {
      "dom_id": "step-q31400",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-31400-a",
