    "q-31399": {
      "dom_id": "step-q31399",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{5}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
