    "q-351285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q351285",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{9}\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{9}\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{3}^{9}{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(16-4) \\\\  & =(12)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
