    "q-49517": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49517",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} & ={\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
